Title: Hereford campervan family cheers Lionesses to victory
Date: 2025-07-14
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [{'Speaker': 'Kevin Morris', 'Text': 'As soon as the game started, they put on another great performance and blew away Wales,', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 3, 'StartChar': 88, 'EndChar': 154}}, {'Speaker': 'Kevin Morris', 'Text': 'It was just busy coming out of the stadium, said Mr Morris. "We got on to the one train station, we couldn\'t get on to the train. The next one came in. We changed for our last train and then just stopped in the middle of nowhere.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 6, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 230}}, {'Speaker': 'Kevin Morris', 'Text': 'We were there for about 20 or 30 minutes and we were told to get off and a bus would turn up.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 7, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 86}}, {'Speaker': 'Kevin Morris', 'Text': "A bus did turn up but then it went everywhere, before we got back to where we're staying in Arbon, just on the side of Lake Constance.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 8, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 116}}, {'Speaker': 'Kevin Morris', 'Text': 'I think we can do it again.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 11, 'StartChar': 23, 'EndChar': 51}}, {'Speaker': 'Kevin Morris', 'Text': 'He said he hoped they would be "lucky enough to get through to see the semi-final", particularly as the family set off on their journey back to Hereford on 24 July.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 12, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 135}}], 'Description': [{'Description': "A family who travelled 800 miles (1,280 km) in their campervan to cheer on England against Wales in the UEFA Women's Euros were jubilant after they won 6-1.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 1, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 137}}, {'Description': 'The Morris family drove from Hereford to watch the Lionesses book their place in the quarter-finals after their outstanding victory at the St Gallen stadium in Switzerland on Sunday.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 2, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 161}}, {'Description': 'Kevin Morris, who was in the stadium with his wife, Kelly, daughter, Amelia, 16, and son, Ethan, 13, said the atmosphere was "great".', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 3, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 87}}, {'Description': 'Mr Morris spoke to BBC Radio Hereford & Worcester as the rest of the family caught up on their sleep after a late night getting to and from the stadium, but he said it was "worth it".', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 5, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 176}}, {'Description': 'They are staying in their campervan at Arbon near Lake Constance, which is where the borders of Germany, Austria and Switzerland meet.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 6, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 106}}, {'Description': 'Their onwards journey took them to Paris, Courgenay and Zurich, where they watched England play the Netherlands, and then Arbon.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 10, 'StartChar': 93, 'EndChar': 190}}, {'Description': 'On Tuesday, the family will drive their campervan back to Zurich, where they will watch England take on Sweden in the quarter-final on Thursday (20:00 BST) in a repeat of the Euro 2022 semi-final.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 11, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 154}}], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': 'Kevin, Amelia, Ethan and Kelly are standing in a line wearing football tops.'}]}
